<rml>
<head>
	<title>MU Helper Skill Picker</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="base.rcss"/>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="skill_icons.rcss"/>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="master_skill_icons.rcss"/>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="mu_helper_skill_picker.rcss"/>
</head>
<body>
	<!-- The flyout beside the MU Helper config window's attack/buff slots. Docked-right like its
	     owner, so #panel carries the same root transform, anchored at the dock's own origin: every
	     entry's left/top is native's reference-space fan-out position, computed in C++
	     (CMuHelperSkillPicker::LayoutPlacements()) because it is a genuinely computed layout.

	     Each icon is one named cell of a generated skill atlas (skill_icons.rcss, master_skill_icons.rcss), bound as a whole
	     decorator -- the only way to crop an atlas in this build. -->
	<div id="panel" data-model="mu_helper_skill_picker"
	     data-style-left="root_x + 'px'" data-style-top="root_y + 'px'"
	     data-style-transform="'scale(' + root_scale + ')'">
		<div class="mhsp-entry slot slot--filled" data-for="e : entries"
		     data-style-left="e.left + 'px'" data-style-top="e.top + 'px'">
			<div class="mhsp-icon" data-style-decorator="e.decorator"></div>
		</div>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
